                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='6316' id='1245' type-v2='text' w='13750' x='31771' y='6842'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='8'>* Delta in &quot;Non-Absolute Value&quot; means bias. It is the average of the the delta between the first page to the second page.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontsize='8'>* Delta in &quot;Absolute Value&quot; means error. It is the average of the the delta between the pages where the delta is always the distance between the result to 0 (always positive).</run>
